1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:16,125
I am the teacher. I explain things in plain words: a sentence that lost you, in a minute; a method or a paper, in one sitting; a whole subject, over weeks. I answer to Feynman.

2
00:00:16,549 --> 00:00:24,383
When a sentence Claude Code just wrote lost you, I say it again in plain words, in under a minute.

3
00:00:24,383 --> 00:00:45,660
I explain a method or a paper in one sitting: in chat, or on request as a page where you mark what lost you, ending in a short quiz that grades itself. For a subject that takes weeks, I run a course in your own session, with lessons that remember what you have learned.

4
00:00:46,049 --> 00:01:09,209
I work by Feynman's rule: if it cannot be said simply, it is not understood yet. AI loves jargon, and jargon is where a reader gets lost. So I allow myself at most three technical terms, each defined, and when I cannot honestly explain, I say Gap rather than sound fluent.

5
00:01:09,209 --> 00:01:23,705
I show a real image or a video I have checked before drawing anything, and I link only to what I have actually opened. A debrief stays offline, because your session is private.

6
00:01:24,099 --> 00:01:33,094
A real run. A wet-lab biologist asks what a permutation test is, and why the example uses five thousand of them.

7
00:01:33,094 --> 00:01:45,936
My answer is Explained: short bullets, each term defined, the real numbers from the analysis, which I re-ran, and a takeaway for the next problem.

8
00:01:46,349 --> 00:01:57,620
On a page I would also draw it. Serum colonies on the left, controls on the right, and the real gap between their averages, nearly one millimetre.

9
00:01:57,620 --> 00:02:09,401
If serum did nothing, the labels would not matter. So I shuffle them, measure the gap again, and add it to the pile. Again and again, five thousand times.

10
00:02:09,401 --> 00:02:27,048
The pile is what chance alone produces. The real gap sits far out on the right, reached once in five thousand shuffles. That is the whole test; the quiz asks what fifty shuffles would change.

11
00:02:27,449 --> 00:02:42,238
Three things to type: debrief, at the sentence that lost you; explain, with the method or paper, adding 'as a page' for the figure and the quiz; and course, with the subject.

12
00:02:42,649 --> 00:02:47,836
The first line is Explained, or Gap when I cannot honestly deliver.

13
00:02:47,836 --> 00:02:59,842
Say who it is for when you type your request, such as a wet-lab biologist; otherwise I write for a colleague from a neighbouring field.
